  "description": "spec/execution-model.md:635-647's own worked example, verbatim: a scope lives as long as any handler registered inside it may still run, so `setup`'s frame — and the `:speed` parameter in it — is still reachable when the handler fires after the call has returned, and the program prints `10`. Going out of scope is visibility, not destruction (spec/execution-model.md:371-376). A runtime whose handler does not keep the registering frame raises `ol-undefined-var` on `:speed` here instead — measured.",
